        {
          "slug": "research-animal-facility-management",
          "reason": "Official Prisma schema and API sources evidence the four core structures: Animal records carry internalId, species, strain, genotype, sex, birth/arrival dates, status and identifiers; Room, Rack and Cage models provide capacity, position and occupancy status; breeding, litter/weaning, health, medication and death-report records provide the census-and-disposition loop; Protocol records carry IACUC number, status, animalLimit and version, while Animal.protocolId and the protocols API animalCount provide research-use linkage. README confirms a React/Hono/Prisma/PostgreSQL web application with Docker self-hosting and an Apache-2.0 community edition limited to 500 animals per lab. Cage moves are applied through the animal's current cage assignment rather than a separate movement-history event, protocol amendments are not separately modeled, and animal status is operational rather than an explicit newborn/weaned life-stage; those limits are recorded in the research note.",
